SUMMARY:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens Fall Plant Sale & FundraiserHallberg Butterfly Gardens Fall Plant Sale & Fundraiser
DESCRIPTION:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens’ Fall Native Plant Sale & Fundraiser is coming up October 2nd & 3rd\, from 9:00 am–4:00 pm!\nOur nursery focuses on California native plants that support local wildlife and pollinators—especially butterflies and moths. Whether you’re adding a few natives to your garden\, creating a backyard wildlife habitat\, or looking for host and nectar plants\, we’ll have a wide variety to choose from.\nFall is an excellent time to plant California native plants.  This year’s sale will include red-flowering currant\, seaside daisy\, Douglas iris\, Dutchman’s pipevine\, western azalea\, blue elderberry\, tiger lily\, hedgerow plants\, and much more.\nPlant lists organized by bloom time and butterfly and moth host plants will be available at the sale\, and our knowledgeable staff will be on hand to help answer questions and help you choose plants for your garden.\nBecause parking at Hallberg Butterfly Gardens is limited\, the plant sale is by appointment.\nReserve a time and view the complete plant list on our website: https://hallbergbutterflygardens.org/our-nursery\nAfter your nursery appointment\, you’re welcome to stay and enjoy a self-guided walk through the Gardens.\nYour plant purchases support Hallberg Butterfly Gardens and our work creating and caring for habitat for butterflies\, moths\, pollinators\, and other local wildlife.\nWe hope to see you at the Gardens!
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/hallberg-butterfly-gardens-fall-plant-sale-fundraiserhallberg-butterfly-gardens-fall-plant-sale-fundraiser/2026-10-03/
LOCATION:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens\, 8687 Oak Grove Avenue\, Sebastopol\, CA\, 95472\, United States
CATEGORIES:Fundraiser
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Hallberg-Butterfly-Gardens-Fall-Plant-Sale-Fundraiser.jpg
GEO:38.4304091;-122.8650148
